Please describe the bug 🐞
When we use Tabular with the Iceberg rest catalog, the namespaceExists returned false even if the namespace is created.
Code example
        if (catalog instanceof SupportsNamespaces catalogNs) {
            boolean b = catalogNs.namespaceExists(Namespace.of("public", "default"));
//            Map<String, String> meta = catalogNs.loadNamespaceMetadata(Namespace.of("public", "default"));
//            System.out.println(meta);

            catalogNs.createNamespace(Namespace.of("public", "default"));
            for (Namespace listNamespace : catalogNs.listNamespaces()) {
                System.out.println(listNamespace.toString());
// we can list the namespace public.default here
            }
            boolean b = catalogNs.namespaceExists(Namespace.of("public", "default"));
           // the b is false, because the request uses an encoded name to query, the request will encode the namespace to public%1default.

            System.out.println(catalogNs.loadNamespaceMetadata(Namespace.of("public.default")));
            // returns true here.
        }

We expected using the Namespace.of("public", "default") also can check the namespace existence and get the namespace metadata.

